b8280-7169-5501-91ed-dca90eb21eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340805/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f691013-78ed-50c3-bcc8-28eff43c37bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340805/field-1/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :answer-field/choices ["q-340805/field-1/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" "q-340805/field-1/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340805/field-2/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :answer/id #uuid "6f40bf76-2ca5-5fdb-aa42-0e4983bd5f31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340805/field-2/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa" :answer/id #uuid "95426d33-5078-5aac-a53c-9063b70b0548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340805/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "61ee9948-5773-5725-bd42-ffb431e4e1f0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340805/field-2/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :answer-field/choices ["q-340805/field-2/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" "q-340805/field-2/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340805" :question/id #uuid "1c9712b7-d767-5e8a-8b70-ecda1f55bedd" :question/math-academy-id "q-340805" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340805/field-1" "q-340805/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340805"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/field-1/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :answer/id #uuid "e636dee2-d854-56e0-a449-a8034dcffd79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/field-1/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" :answer/id #uuid "503e9788-7072-5cd9-b602-242198537163" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebf55ae-fce2-5537-b10d-2e2e812609ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340806/field-1/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be9